<section>
  <grid spacing="none">
    <grid-item>
      <h2>Expansion cools the cosmos</h2>
      <p><b>As the universe expands, it cools—and what matter and light can do changes.</b> Follow the sequence in the log; each stage depends on the conditions before it.</p>
      <smart-layout orientation="horizontal" variant="minimalTimeline">
        <smart-layout-item>
          <h4>Expansion and cooling</h4>
          <p>Growing distances accompany falling temperature.</p>
        </smart-layout-item>
        <smart-layout-item>
          <h4>Early · Nuclei form</h4>
          <p>Atomic nuclei can persist as conditions cool.</p>
        </smart-layout-item>
        <smart-layout-item>
          <h4>About 380,000 years</h4>
          <p>Neutral atoms form; light can travel freely.</p>
        </smart-layout-item>
        <smart-layout-item>
          <h4>Later · Structure emerges</h4>
          <p>Stars and galaxies develop over cosmic time.</p>
        </smart-layout-item>
      </smart-layout>
    </grid-item>
  </grid>
</section>